# 🐳 Docker Commands Cheat Sheet

A simple guide to learn Docker commands with easy explanations.

## 1. Basic Commands

| Command            | Use                     |
| ------------------ | ----------------------- |
| `docker --version` | Check Docker version    |
| `docker info`      | Show Docker information |
| `docker help`      | Show help               |
| `docker ps`        | Show running containers |
| `docker ps -a`     | Show all containers     |

## 2. Docker Image Commands

| Command                      | Use                  |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------- |
| `docker images`              | Show all images      |
| `docker pull nginx`          | Download an image    |
| `docker build -t myapp .`    | Build an image       |
| `docker rmi nginx`           | Delete an image      |
| `docker image inspect nginx` | Show image details   |
| `docker tag myapp myapp:v1`  | Create an image tag  |
| `docker image prune`         | Remove unused images |

## 3. Docker Container Commands

| Command                      | Use                        |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `docker run nginx`           | Create and run a container |
| `docker run -d nginx`        | Run in background          |
| `docker run -it ubuntu bash` | Open Ubuntu terminal       |
| `docker start CONTAINER`     | Start a container          |
| `docker stop CONTAINER`      | Stop a container           |
| `docker restart CONTAINER`   | Restart a container        |
| `docker rm CONTAINER`        | Delete a container         |
| `docker kill CONTAINER`      | Force stop a container     |
| `docker rename OLD NEW`      | Rename a container         |
| `docker pause CONTAINER`     | Pause a container          |
| `docker unpause CONTAINER`   | Resume a container         |

## 4. Port Mapping Commands

| Command                       | Use                                         |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| `docker run -p 8080:80 nginx` | Connect host port 8080 to container port 80 |
| `docker port CONTAINER`       | Show container ports                        |

## 5. Docker Exec Commands

| Command                          | Use                        |
| -------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| `docker exec -it CONTAINER bash` | Enter container terminal   |
| `docker exec CONTAINER ls`       | List container files       |
| `docker exec CONTAINER pwd`      | Show current directory     |
| `docker exec CONTAINER env`      | Show environment variables |

## 6. Docker Logs Commands

| Command                           | Use                       |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `docker logs CONTAINER`           | Show container logs       |
| `docker logs -f CONTAINER`        | Show live logs            |
| `docker logs --tail 50 CONTAINER` | Show last 50 log lines    |
| `docker stats`                    | Show CPU and memory usage |
| `docker top CONTAINER`            | Show running processes    |

## 7. Docker Hub Commands

| Command                  | Use                        |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------- |
| `docker login`           | Login to Docker Hub        |
| `docker logout`          | Logout from Docker Hub     |
| `docker search nginx`    | Search Docker images       |
| `docker pull nginx`      | Download an image          |
| `docker push USER/IMAGE` | Upload image to Docker Hub |

## 8. Docker Network Commands

| Command                                     | Use                          |
| ------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `docker network ls`                         | Show networks                |
| `docker network create mynet`               | Create a network             |
| `docker network inspect mynet`              | Show network details         |
| `docker network connect mynet CONTAINER`    | Connect container to network |
| `docker network disconnect mynet CONTAINER` | Disconnect container         |
| `docker network rm mynet`                   | Delete network               |

## 9. Docker Volume Commands

| Command                       | Use                   |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `docker volume ls`            | Show volumes          |
| `docker volume create myvol`  | Create volume         |
| `docker volume inspect myvol` | Show volume details   |
| `docker volume rm myvol`      | Delete volume         |
| `docker volume prune`         | Remove unused volumes |

## 10. Docker Compose Commands

| Command                  | Use                      |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------ |
| `docker compose version` | Check Compose version    |
| `docker compose up`      | Start services           |
| `docker compose up -d`   | Start in background      |
| `docker compose down`    | Stop and remove services |
| `docker compose ps`      | Show services            |
| `docker compose logs`    | Show logs                |
| `docker compose build`   | Build services           |
| `docker compose restart` | Restart services         |
| `docker compose pull`    | Download service images  |

## 11. Docker System Commands

| Command                  | Use                       |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| `docker system df`       | Show disk usage           |
| `docker system info`     | Show system information   |
| `docker system events`   | Show Docker events        |
| `docker system prune`    | Remove unused Docker data |
| `docker container prune` | Remove stopped containers |
| `docker network prune`   | Remove unused networks    |

**Warning:** Cleanup commands can delete Docker resources. Check before executing them.

## 12. Dockerfile Instructions

| Instruction  | Use                            |
| ------------ | ------------------------------ |
| `FROM`       | Select base image              |
| `RUN`        | Execute build commands         |
| `CMD`        | Set default command            |
| `ENTRYPOINT` | Set main application command   |
| `COPY`       | Copy files                     |
| `ADD`        | Copy files with extra features |
| `WORKDIR`    | Set working directory          |
| `EXPOSE`     | Document container port        |
| `ENV`        | Set environment variables      |
| `ARG`        | Set build arguments            |
| `USER`       | Set container user             |
| `VOLUME`     | Define storage location        |
| `LABEL`      | Add image information          |

## 13. Simple Docker Practical

**Step 1: Download Nginx**

```bash
docker pull nginx
```

**Step 2: Run Container**

```bash
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name mywebsite nginx
```

**Step 3: Check Container**

```bash
docker ps
```

**Step 4: Open Browser**

```text
http://localhost:8080
```

**Step 5: Check Logs**

```bash
docker logs mywebsite
```

**Step 6: Stop Container**

```bash
docker stop mywebsite
```

**Step 7: Remove Container**

```bash
docker rm mywebsite
```

